                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="452" value="This can only happen when someone was injected directly into the particiapnt set off-chain as part of a normal state transition - e.g. a friend sends funds to a friend directly off-chain. The on-chain system is NOT AWARE of the expansion of the participant set, and allows a dispute to be commited without accouting the new participant.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This isn&#39;t really a problem, since the participan that can&#39;t audit never commited funds and the funds are not actually theirs, but from the &#39;friend&#39; and the frend can audit and provide the peer data to audit retroactively, but in the worst case the peer can walk away without actually indoorig any financial loss since the funds where never theirs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Once the off-chain transaction to update the participant set is final, the peer can update the snapshot on-chain -&amp;gt; which would include them in the particpant set and the chain would gurantee them DA going forward.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If the funds were theirs and they came as a legitimate L1 deposit, the chain IS AWARE and enforces their siganture requirement OR data availability.guarantees." style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="451">
                    <mxGeometry y="30" width="300" height="380" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="453" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="dv-frame" source="447" target="450">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="1620" y="740" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="1700" y="740" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
